<!--
  HILDA initial outreach -- table format per architect 2026-06-28.
  Owner edits the `status` and `owner_status_note` cells inline. Reply parsing
  is structural (header row text + cell index), so attribute stripping by
  email clients is non-fatal. batch_id is embedded both in the subject and in
  a tagged span at the top so the inbound parser can correlate the reply back
  to the outreach.
-->
<html>
<body style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;">

<p>Hello {{ owner.owner_name or "Owner" }},</p>

<p>Please update the status of work items assigned to you.</p>

<!--
  Tagged anchor: keeps the BATCH-id correlation findable even when the owner
  edits the table or strips formatting. The inbound parser looks for the
  literal "HILDA-BATCH-ID:" token + the BATCH-<id> value.
-->
<p style="font-size: 12px; color: #666;">
  HILDA-BATCH-ID: {{ batch_id }}
</p>

<table border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0"
       style="border-collapse: collapse; margin: 12px 0;">
  <thead style="background-color: #f0f0f0;">
    <tr>
      <th align="left">Item No</th>
      <th align="left">Item Title</th>
      <th align="left">Current Status</th>
      <th align="left">Completion Date</th>
      <th align="left">Owner Comment</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for it in items %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ it.item_no }}</td>
      <td>{{ it.item_name or it.get("item_title", "") }}</td>
      <td>Open</td>
      <td>&nbsp;</td>
      <td>&nbsp;</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<p><strong>Current Status</strong> values: Open / Closed / Blocked / Delayed</p>

<ul style="font-size: 13px; color: #555;">
  <li><strong>Open</strong> &mdash; still working; leave as-is or add a note.</li>
  <li><strong>Closed</strong> &mdash; you confirm the work is done. Please fill
      <em>Completion Date</em> with the date the work finished
      (format: <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code> preferred, e.g. <code>2026-08-15</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Blocked</strong> &mdash; cannot proceed; please add the blocker in
      <em>Owner Comment</em>.</li>
  <li><strong>Delayed</strong> &mdash; running late; please add an ETA in
      <em>Owner Comment</em>.</li>
</ul>

<p>Thanks.</p>

</body>
</html>
